WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.959
ALISON GOPNIK: If you look at our history, I think what
will happen is that will change in all

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:08.069
sorts of serious, important ways, and we
won't notice it. Because what always

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:12.269
happens is that the day before you're
born is always Eden and the things that

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:16.949
happen to you in your own lifespan are
always technology and the day after your

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:21.270
children are born is always 'Mad Max,'
right? So we always are in this situation

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.650
where we think that the things that
happen to us are technological

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.550
innovations, and they're probably going
to end up being Mad Max. But then, of

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.940
course, if we think about the things like
the fact that in this room there are

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.140
right angles everywhere, it's not like
we're really sitting there saying, "My God,

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:47.610
the right angles! The right angles are
taking over everywhere we look!" Even though the

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.690
fact of right angles has made enormous
changes in our lives. Or the fact that

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.920
there's print everywhere doesn't strike
us as being something that's this weird

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.520
technology, that we're constantly getting
distracted because we have to figure out

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.650
what that 'R' is, right? That's just, that's
just part of our lives. And I suspect

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:08.400
what will happen is we'll change in
really deep and profound ways, and we

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.549
won't notice it, because it'll be
happening over and across generations.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:13.530
KEVIN KELLY: That's fantastic, thank you.

